From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emil Popovic <mail@emilpopovic.me>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Give character_length a default so it does not infer a latch

character_length is assigned only inside the `if (reg_read_i.fcr.fifo_en)`
branch of the RX always_comb, unlike tl_characters and timeout_level which
are defaulted with the rest of the block. It holds its value when the FIFO
is disabled, so synthesis infers a latch and Yosys reports a combinational
loop through it.

The value is only read inside the same branch that assigns it, so the
behaviour is already correct; this only removes the latch.
---
 obi_uart_rx.sv | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/obi_uart_rx.sv b/obi_uart_rx.sv
index 948a04e..6d1bce7 100644
--- a/obi_uart_rx.sv
+++ b/obi_uart_rx.sv
@@ -215,6 +215,7 @@ module obi_uart_rx import obi_uart_pkg::*; #()
 
     timeout_count_d = timeout_count_q;
     timeout_o         = 1'b0; // timeout_o
+    character_length = '0;
     timeout_level = '0;
 
     fifo_error_index_d = fifo_error_index_q; // FIFO Error
-- 
